## Context

Reading-3 (tracker [[0605]]). Table 1 = `tbl:status-difficulty` (§7.1,
caption `slides/manuscript/main.tex:872`, body
`\input tab_status_difficulty_en.tex`, emitter
`src/aedist/tabulate_status_difficulty.py`). Current columns: Status, n,
Share of list, Avg. detection prob. (Exp 1, all models). Three parts.

## A. Caption (concrete)

Replace the caption (`:872`) with:

> Composition of the reference list by asset lifecycle status, from
> Proposed to Retired, and detection likelihood. Experiment 1 includes
> all models; Experiment 2 is the single-shot with-documents arm.
> Source: author.

(Use "single-shot with-documents" per [[0620]]; this is arm 3 / 1D.)

## B. Add an Exp 2 arm-3 detection-likelihood column (ENGINEERING — heaviest part)

The table now has ONE detection column (Exp 1, all models). Add a SECOND:
detection likelihood from **Exp 2 arm 3** (single-shot, with documents,
1D). So the table contrasts Exp 1 (all models, memory-only) vs Exp 2
docs-arm per-status detection.
- The emitter currently reads Exp 1 only (`exp1_recognition`,
  `experiments/outputs/exp1_batch2/*.record.json`). Wire in the Exp 2
  arm-3 records and compute per-status detection probability the SAME way
  (mean over (plant × run) cells). Check whether an `exp2_recognition`
  path exists or must be built; if the arm-3 recognition data is not
  readily available, this part may split into its own sub-child of 0605.
- Regenerate BOTH `tab_status_difficulty_en.tex` and the FR version via
  the `render.mk` target; commit them. Numbers are macro/artifact-sourced
  (derive-from-artifact); do not hand-type.
- Column header for the new one e.g. "Avg. detection prob. (Exp 2, docs)"
  and rename the existing to "(Exp 1, all models)" so the two are
  distinguished.

## C. Split the §7.1 text into two themes

Currently §7.1 (`:863–868`) mixes the register shape and the detection
result. Separate them:
1. **The register (shape of the list):** it is a fast-growing country
   situation — proposed and planned plants dominate the list; state the
   policy and business relevance of getting this right. Soften the
   absolute: `:865` "parametric memory \emph{cannot} know them" →
   "**hard to know**" (not an absolute "cannot").
2. **Detection likelihood:** define it explicitly — the probability that a
   random plant in a status category is found by a random run in the
   experiment (random plant × random run). Then the finding: the
   operational category is easy (note Exp 1 includes weak models, yet they
   still find operational plants), while the long tail (proposed/planned)
   is hard. With the two columns (B), contrast Exp 1 vs Exp 2-docs.

